2026-11-07T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-2446) 'A2A hardening leaves five verification gaps open
 # uuid: c453877a-0ad6-566f-b8c6-21454754fcb5
 # tags: rfd:title
 RFD:Discussion  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-11-07T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2446) 'a record of five checks a security pass never ran, so the pass is not called finished.
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2446  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2446) 'the MCP-to-A2A bridge server, and the Godot editor's MCP listener and its new A2A route.
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2446  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2446) 'Can a security pass call itself finished while five of its own claims stay unchecked?
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2446  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2446) 'Eight pull requests closed a prompt-injection finding, moved a bridge server and an editor
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2446  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2446) 'listener to the Agent2Agent protocol's 1.0 wire format, and closed a browser-origin hole in
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2446  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2446) 'both of the listener's protocols. Every pull request carries tests that passed on one machine.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2446  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2446) 'Read the five gaps below before picking any of this work back up, and close one gap at a time.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2446  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2446) 'A2A hardening leaves five verification gaps open
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2446  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2446) 'Five verification gaps stay open, and work on them does not resume until this record changes.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2446  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2446) '- No diff against the operator's own A2A listener script, which was never recovered.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2446  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2446) '- No run on the Windows desk or inside the resident editor session the operator described.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2446  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2446) '- No run against the Agent2Agent protocol's conformance suite, for either system.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2446  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2446) '- No real browser has exercised the new Origin refusal, only a forged command-line header.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2446  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2446) '- Both systems' test commands still force a hidden display, against the windowed-test rule.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2446  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2446) '- No earlier RFD names either system; this is their first register entry.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2446  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2446) 'The five gaps, and what closes each one
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2446  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2446) '- Godot parity. The operator ran a resident editor with an uncommitted listener script added
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2446  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2446) '  to its MCP addon, serving A2A at one address with a card and two commands. That script was
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2446  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2446) '  never pushed anywhere and could not be found on any branch, so the listener that shipped is
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2446  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2446) '  a clean-room build from the protocol specification, not a check against the original. Closes
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2446  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2446) '  when that original script is pushed to a branch and the two are diffed line by line.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2446  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2446) '- The Windows desk. Every check so far ran on a Mac, in a real window, never headless. Closes
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2446  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2446) '  when the same checks run once on the desk, inside the resident editor session.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2446  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2446) '- A conformance suite. Both systems were checked against the official client library and
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2446  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2446) '  against each other, never against the protocol's own conformance suite. Closes when that
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2446  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2446) '  suite is identified by name and run once against each system, with its own report kept.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2446  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2446) '- A real browser. The Origin refusal was proven with a command-line client sending a forged
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2446  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2446) '  header, never with a browser tab. Closes when an actual browser page, opened by a person,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2446  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2446) '  is shown the refusal.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2446  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2446) '- The hidden-display test commands. Both systems' committed test commands still pass a flag
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2446  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2446) '  that hides the window, against the rule that a Godot test runs where it can be watched.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2446  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2446) '  Every check in this pass ran windowed by hand instead, by overriding the command each time.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2446  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2446) '  Closes when the committed command itself drops the flag and still passes.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2446  1 LINE
 Text:Written
